// esc_val2's condition: whether the escape is octal. Named out because the
// if/else in c2.id already spends the whole 3-action budget on c=0, if and
// else, leaving no room to name charat(s, 1) before the condition. chr/ has
// no room for a sibling file, so c2.id was promoted into this directory.

is_oct_esc(string s) {
  int ch1 = charat(s, 1);
  int d = dig_val(ch1);
  int ok = d >= 0 && d < 8;
} return int ok;
("\\101"):(1)
("\\n"):(0)
